# 高频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List06核心词汇

{{isolate}}{/ˈaɪsəleɪt/}{隔离；孤立}{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of infection.}}
{{justify}}{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/}{证明...正当}{The decision was justified by the circumstances.}}
{{launch}}{/lɔːntʃ/}{发射；启动}{The company launched a new initiative to reduce waste.}}
{{maintain}}{/meɪnˈteɪn/}{维持；维护}{It is difficult to maintain a work-life balance.}}
{{measure}}{/ˈmeʒər/}{测量；措施}{The government introduced new measures to combat crime.}}
{{mechanism}}{/ˈmekənɪzəm/}{机制；机械装置}{The brain has a natural mechanism for regulating temperature.}}
{{mental}}{/ˈmentl/}{精神的；心理的}{Mental health awareness has increased significantly.}}
{{method}}{/ˈmeθəd/}{方法；办法}{The research method used in the study was rigorous.}}
{{monitor}}{/ˈmɒnɪtər/}{监控；监视}{The system monitors air quality in real time.}}
{{moral}}{/ˈmɒrəl/}{道德的；道义的}{There are moral questions surrounding the use of AI.}}
{{motivate}}{/ˈməʊtɪveɪt/}{激励；激发}{The scholarship motivated students to work harder.}}
{{mutual}}{/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/}{相互的；共同的}{The agreement was based on mutual benefit.}}
{{negative}}{/ˈneɡətɪv/}{消极的；否定的}{Negative feedback can be constructive if delivered properly.}}
{{negotiate}}{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt/}{谈判；协商}{The two sides negotiated a peace agreement.}}
{{network}}{/ˈnetwɜːk/}{网络；网状系统}{A strong professional network opens doors to new opportunities.}}
{{notion}}{/ˈnəʊʃn/}{概念；想法}{The notion of universal basic income is gaining support.}}
{{obtain}}{/əbˈteɪn/}{获得；得到}{The data was obtained through a comprehensive survey.}}
{{obvious}}{/ˈɒbviəs/}{明显的；显而易见的}{The benefits of exercise are obvious.}}
{{occupy}}{/ˈɒkjupaɪ/}{占据；占领}{The building occupies an entire city block.}}
{{occur}}{/əˈkɜːr/}{发生；出现}{Serious side effects rarely occur with this medication.}}
{{operate}}{/ˈɒpəreɪt/}{操作；经营}{The factory operates 24 hours a day.}}
{{opportunity}}{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti/}{机会；时机}{This internship is a great opportunity for students.}}
{{oppose}}{/əˈpəʊz/}{反对；对抗}{Several lawmakers opposed the proposed amendment.}}
{{option}}{/ˈɒpʃn/}{选项；选择权}{Customers have the option to cancel at any time.}}
{{orient}}{/ˈɔːrient/}{使适应；朝向}{The program is designed to orient new employees.}}
{{outline}}{/ˈaʊtlaɪn/}{大纲；概述}{The professor outlined the main topics for the course.}}
{{overall}}{/ˌəʊvərˈɔːl/}{总体的；全面的}{Overall, the project was a great success.}}
{{overcome}}{/ˌəʊvəˈkʌm/}{克服；战胜}{She overcame many obstacles to reach her goal.}}
{{overlook}}{/ˌəʊvəˈlʊk/}{忽略；俯瞰}{Important details were overlooked during the review.}}
{{overwhelming}}{/ˌəʊvəˈwelmɪŋ/}{压倒性的；势不可挡的}{The response to the campaign was overwhelming.}}
